<title>USA: USLIFE chairman refuses answers during call.</title>
<headline>USLIFE chairman refuses answers during call.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>USLIFE Corp Chairman Gordon Crosby on Thursday refused to answer a number of key questions about the company's proposed $1.8 billion merger with American General Corp in a tense conference call with investors Thursday morning.</p>
<p>Crosby, who has been chairman of USLIFE for 30 years, repeatedly declined to give information about projected cost savings from a merger, plans for senior management and details about how the deal was struck.</p>
</text>
